    "updated_at": "2026-01-16T19:11:50Z",
    "body": "I'm running into the issue now with evcc.io. \n\nMy local is set to en_NL. But whatwg in Safari on macOS reads it as:\n```\n> navigator.language\nnavigator.languages\nnew Intl.DateTimeFormat(undefined, { hour: \"numeric\", minute: \"numeric\" }).format(new Date())\nnew Intl.DateTimeFormat(undefined, { hour: \"numeric\", minute: \"numeric\" }).resolvedOptions()\n< {locale: \"en-US\", calendar: \"gregory\", numberingSystem: \"latn\", timeZone: \"Europe/Amsterdam\", hourCycle: \"h12\", …}\n```\nWhich results in a 12h time picker:\n\n<img width=\"843\" height=\"791\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0a54c4b2-efab-4ce6-b0e9-fe565d63b539\" />\n\n\n\n\n<img width=\"495\" height=\"461\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/18a4aa1c-4ab1-4fe5-8f94-cb4691601f84\" />\n<img width=\"471\" height=\"297\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/73bc1ae5-832d-43c8-a714-c40ca6e1c55b\" />",
